Package: forsci
Title: Forensic Scientometrics: Integrity Signals in Publication Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Detects statistical and textual signals that may deserve a closer
    look in collections of scientific publications, and documents the
    evidence behind them: retraction rates, journal-to-journal citation
    stacking, template titles, tortured phrases and unusual productivity,
    with a module for paper mill screening. Every result carries an evidence
    level (signal, pattern, documentary, established) and its alternative
    explanations; a signal is never presented as proof of misconduct, and
    individuals are not ranked. Reads OpenAlex responses and the Retraction
    Watch database, includes a simulated benchmark with known outcomes to
    validate the methods, and writes reproducible case reports.
